Throughout this Award in Sports Media, the participants experience a range of opportunities to develop a spectrum of sports media-specific competencies as well as transferable skills. These diverse skills are essential to fulfill the wide spectrum of formats characterising sports media. 

In the first part of the course, the students are provided with the necessary basic background needed to embed the rest of the course material. The students are in fact here introduced to the history of sports and the parallel evolution of sports media in the Maltese Islands. 

It’s important that journalists keep to the facts and maintain high ethical standards. Ethical considerations apply in sports media, just as much in the regular media, and key issues for consideration include privacy, the portrayal of women’s sports and the use of social media. A basic grounding in media law, image rights, fairness and impartiality is also given.
The learner will be able to: 
a) define key terminology used in sports journalism and media;
b) describe the development of sports and sports journalism in Malta;
c) understand basic concepts and theories of sports journalism;
d) list the main principles underlying ethical sports journalism;
e) name national and international bodies responsible for maintaining standards in sports journalism; 
f) list new trends in sports journalism and sports media technology;

g) identify the qualities of a professional photographer and that of a high-quality sports photograph/photo report.
h) label a professional camera used for sports photography.
i) write sports articles
j) perform sports interviews The learner will be able to: 

a) demonstrate knowledge of the history of sports and sports journalism, ethical standards, sports reporting (including photo reporting) and interviewing.
b) demonstrate knowledge of  good conduct in sports journalism
c) apply ethical principles related to sports journalism in the sports organisations they represent.
d) create sports communications on the latest sports  news issues and using contemporary media technology.
e) operate a photographic camera.
f) apply practice tips learnt during this programme to take good quality sports event photos.
